+/**
+ * Rebinds the runtime, its maps and its projections to the calling thread.
+ *
+ * Owner-thread affinity assumes the embedder controls which OS thread its work
+ * runs on. Runtimes with managed concurrency do not: a Dart isolate, a Go
+ * goroutine or a .NET task can resume on a different pool thread between two
+ * calls, through no action of the caller. Calling this first re-homes the
+ * affinity to the thread the caller is actually on.
+ *
+ * Render sessions are deliberately NOT included. A session's owner is the
+ * thread that attached it, which may be a display-paced render thread that has
+ * nothing to do with the thread driving the map, so re-homing sessions here
+ * would take them from whoever is rendering. Use
+ * mln_render_session_rebind_thread for those, one session at a time.
+ *
+ * Contract:
+ * - No call on the runtime or any of its handles may be in flight.
+ * - The calling thread must not own another live runtime.
+ * - Map projections carry no owner link and are re-homed together with the
+ *   maps: the process is assumed to hold a single live runtime.
+ *
+ * Returns:
+ * - MLN_STATUS_OK on success (or when already bound to the calling thread).
+ * - MLN_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT when runtime is null or not a live handle.
+ * - MLN_STATUS_INVALID_STATE when the calling thread owns another runtime.
+ * - MLN_STATUS_NATIVE_ERROR when an internal exception is converted to status.
+ */
+MLN_API mln_status mln_runtime_rebind_thread(mln_runtime runtime) MLN_NOEXCEPT;
